================================================================================
ARCHITECTURE / PARITY NOTES
================================================================================
* Data binds through the `@Observable ChargingDetailPageModel` (ADR-004 -- no networking in the
  view); the four web hooks map 1:1 to the `ChargingDetailDataSource` seam:
    useChargingSessionDetail   -> loadSession(sessionID)         GET /charging/{id}
    useChargeTelemetry         -> loadTelemetry(sessionID)       GET /charging/{sessionId}/telemetry
    useVehicle                 -> loadVehicle(vehicleID)         GET /vehicles/{id}
    useChargingTelemetryLatest -> loadLatestTelemetry(vehicleID) GET /charging-telemetry/latest
* Everything is stored SI (Wh/W/m/degC/V/A) and converted only at the render boundary via the
  shared `Units` facade (P1/S5) + `TS*` SI formatters (ADR-005). No non-SI is stored/computed.
* Charts use the P3 native Swift Charts wrappers only (TSAreaChart / TSLineChart) -- never a web
  view. The 5 hero RadialGauges use a feature-local `ChargingMetricGauge` (token-built ring) so the
  absolute value+unit render like the web gauge (the shared TSRadialGauge only shows a percentage).
* Navigation: `/charging/:id` is modeled as a typed NavigationDestination
  (`ChargingDetailLink(sessionID:)` + `.chargingDetailDestination()`), mirroring the accepted
  unrouted/detail precedent `AutomationCard*` -- no widening of the value-less `AppRoute` enum.
* Adaptive macOS + iOS (ADR-002/006): gauge/stat grids reflow (LazyVGrid adaptive columns), the
  system back button replaces the web back link; light/dark + Dynamic Type + VoiceOver honored.
* Three data states implemented for every source: loading -> redaction skeleton; empty ->
  ContentUnavailableView per chart/panel (EmptyChargingDetailDataSource); error -> retry surface;
  success -> SampleChargingDetailDataSource.

